RustyRig experimental Windows x64 port
======================================

STATUS: NOT BUILDABLE OR TESTED AS A NATIVE WINDOWS RELEASE (November 2026).
These are packaging/build handoff files, NOT evidence of a working Windows
client. Linux/Devuan remains the supported development platform.

Target: MSYS2 UCRT64 (native MinGW-w64 binaries, NOT the MSYS POSIX runtime).
Do not mix UCRT64, MINGW64 and MSYS libraries in one build. No 32-bit port
is planned as part of this work.

1. Install MSYS2 (https://www.msys2.org/), update its packages as directed
   by MSYS2, then open **MSYS2 UCRT64**.
2. Clone the repository with submodules and enter its root:

       git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/PripyatAutomations/rustyrig-fw.git
       cd rustyrig-fw
       bash rrclient/win32/install-deps.sh

3. Try a native build and **record the first compile/link failure**. There
   is no working Win64 make configuration yet. The POSIX recipes still
   hardcode ELF SONAMEs, .so modules, Unix-only libraries, Unix process
   supervision/PTY facilities, and glib-unix APIs. Expect failures;
   fixing them is the next contributor task. Do NOT mask errors with -i.

4. Once the port can supply these native PE binaries:

       bin/rrclient.exe
       bin/rrclient-gtk.dll
       librustyaxe.dll, librrprotocol.dll, librustyirc.dll,
       libfwdspmgr.dll (or their actual linked dependencies)

   stage a self-contained distribution from the repository root:

       make win64-preflight
       make win64-stage
       make win64-installer

   The stage target invokes tools/win64-stage.sh. It creates
   build/win64-stage with bin/, lib/, share/, config/ and RustyRig.cmd.
   It scans PE imports using objdump, recursively copies MinGW runtime
   DLLs from /ucrt64/bin, and fails on unrecognized missing DLL imports.
   GTK/GStreamer runtime plugins, data and icon themes are also staged.
   No fixed third-party DLL version list is used.

   The installer is build/rustyrig-win64-unsigned.exe by default, and is
   per-user. For an existing stage, makensis can also be called directly
   with /DSTAGE_DIR=<absolute Windows path> and /DOUTFILE=<output path>.
   The GNUmakefile target passes those defines automatically.

5. Installer layout:
       %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\RustyRig\RustyRig.cmd   (launcher)
       %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\RustyRig\bin\rrclient.exe
       %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\RustyRig\bin\rrclient-gtk.dll
       %APPDATA%\rustyrigs\rrclient.cfg

   The first-run config is copied from config/rrclient.cfg.example only
   when absent; it selects the .dll frontend and uses path.modules=./bin.
   The launcher sets its working directory to the installation root.
   Uninstall intentionally preserves the user config and databases.

Outstanding blockers / contributions welcome
---------------------------------------------
- Replace Linux-specific Makefile suffixes/linker flags with native PE
  targets and import libraries. In particular GTK needs the client
  executable's exported API or a shared core DLL; ELF -rdynamic does not
  transfer to PE without work. This is not solved by renaming .so to .dll.
- Port or conditionally disable the POSIX-only pieces in librustyaxe,
  librrprotocol, librustyirc, libfwdspmgr, fwdsp and rrclient. The current
  core uses glib-unix, pty, signals, fork/exec, descriptors and Unix paths.
- Make dynamic frontend loading resolve .dll via native module paths;
  verify Windows TLS/socket behavior before connecting to real sites.
- Check runtime GSettings schemas, icon loaders, GTK themes, GStreamer
  plugins, codec availability and the test configuration on a real Win64
  machine. Plugin search paths and cache files may require relocation.
- Inspect the installer and dependency closure on a clean Windows VM.
  Check Win64 machine architecture, network connection, audio capture/
  playback, foreground/background behavior and cleanup. Sign binaries
  only after such tests; this installer is explicitly unsigned.

For now, send compiler errors and a short environment report (MSYSTEM,
gcc --version, pkg-config --version, make version) with fixes as separate,
reviewable patches. Do not claim the installer or client works merely
because makensis produced an .exe.
